About time, too. First 3.4 ascension, first gnomish wizard ever (all my
wizards were human until now).

I admit that I've been fooling around a lot, trying things out without
really trying to ascend, but this one was too good not to cultivate.

Raisse the Necromancer  St:18/50 Dx:23 Co:18 In:19 Wi:18 Ch:16  Neutral
Astral Plane $:0  HP:200(298) Pw:291(332) AC:-33 Xp:24/45650377 T:59675

Tried frantically to get above 18/50 by eating giants (imagine a gnome
eating a giant...) until I realized that it's the racial maximum.

The AC -33 was because of this: 

 A - a blessed +5 silver dragon scale mail (being worn)
 B - a blessed fireproof +5 pair of speed boots (being worn)
 C - a blessed fireproof +1 cloak of magic resistance (being worn)
 G - a blessed fireproof +5 pair of gauntlets of dexterity (being worn)
 H - a blessed fireproof +2 cornuthaum (being worn)
 O - a blessed +4 Hawaiian shirt (being worn)

 (as well as intrinsic 1 from the friendly coaligned priest on level 15)

Could have had -41 or even lower, I suppose, but it didn't seem
necessary. The silver dragon scale mail was from the only bones file I
hit - a quadruple one, on the second level of the Mines, full of
previous incarnations (and one priestess with spellbooks of light and
identify) dead of impetuosity. This incarnation of Raisse spent a lot
of time sacrificing on level 3 before she even entered the mines,
getting Magicbane (*and* Vorpal Blade *and* Werebane *and* Frost Brand,
and I think also Giantslayer which I sold in a shop; used every type
just enough to get to Basic with it and then wielded nothing but the
Magicbane the whole game) and leveling up enough to lick the rothes and
rabid rats who had offed the others.

Conducts: none, except my usual no-artifact-wishing, no-lifesaving and
no-genocide. I did write a scroll of genocide when I saw all the ; on
the Plane of Water, but never used it and ran to the portal instead.
Polymorph went down the drain by typo, dipping something in an
unidentified potion instead of holy water, but I never polymorphed
myself (didn't even catch lycanthropy).

Ascended with an overstuffed pack, containing among other things a WoW
(1:2). Never needed the other three, and used a blessed magic lamp for
light.

Notable kills: 

The Wizard of Yendor (5 times)

Yes, I thought he was quiet. The only thing I never saw at all in the
game was a tinning kit, but I did eat him once and got teleport control
on top of the teleport control I already had from being a level
twenty-something W. (isn't that a bug?)

Pestilence (thrice)
Famine (5 times)

The second altar was the right one and I never saw Death. Famine was
obnoxious, reviving at my feet when I was wading through ants. Wands of
death took care of him and Pestilence every time, teleportation of the
ants and angels. 

a mastodon

Only one; I'm used to more. Perhaps because after the Valley, it was a
fairly quick game (nearly 60.000 is low-average for me).

23 minotaurs

Those, on the other hand, were a right pain in the behind. Magic
missiles, reflected from the walls, took them out in one most of the
time. Never got crowned, perhaps read a spellbook of finger of death
which was cursed and exploded, or it might have been magic mapping;
those where the only spells I didn't have at the end.

Vlad the Impaler

With a cockatrice corpse, causing the YAFMC I posted a few days ago.

4 Nazguls

And kept and numbered all their rings.

4 disenchanters

Which didn't get a chance to disenchant anything.

a watch captain

Completely by accident because he was in a crowd of Woodland-elves. Lost
telepathy by that, but I was wearing the Eye of the Aethiopica already
(went back to the Mines to get candles after the Quest). Don't know
whether I ever got intrinsic telepathy back, but it seems likely.

3 erinyes

Yay!

16 tengu

The first of which gave me teleportitis at level 11, but I had a ring
from one of the ghosts on the bones level.

47 wraiths

Three left corpses, all in the Valley. The three or four I killed on the
Quest home level when I was still level 13 didn't, worse luck, but
Neferet the Green had a potion of gain level in her chest that I could
get at before she noticed me to speak to.

4 white unicorns
4 black unicorns

And no grey unicorns. Usually I can't avoid killing a few coaligned ones
as collateral damage.

a kobold

Lowest single monster.

Now for another priestess, I suppose, or a cavewoman for a change of
pace.

   Raisse the Demigoddess

